our reasoning if you deny it.\\n\\n---BEGIN USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\nQuestion: Welcome to Double Act AI! Tell us a little about yourself. Who are you and what do you do? Are you a computer expert or are you new to software?\\nResponse: [object Object]\\n\\nQuestion: What are your goals for this project? What led you to pursue this? Where did the idea come from?\\nResponse: My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\n\\nQuestion: What are specific requirements you have in mind? What is your vision for the completed product?\\nResponse: The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\n\\nQuestion: What else should we know about you or your project? Any other context or details you want to share? The system will follow-up with questions automatically when needed.\\nResponse: Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\n\\nQuestion: Do you want a public Home page that introduces the community and links to all sections?\\nResponse: Yes: A welcoming Home page with brief overview, photos, and quick links\\n\\nQuestion: Should we keep your current plan that Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events are resident-only (sign-in required)?\\nResponse: Keep as-is: Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events are resident-only\\n\\nQuestion: How should residents get accounts and be verified?\\nResponse: Residents self-register; an admin approves each account\\n\\nQuestion: For the Dues page, what do you prefer right now?\\nResponse: Accept online payments from residents (with payment history)\\n\\nQuestion: For the Annual Meetings page, what should it include?\\nResponse: Dates plus downloadable agendas and minutes (PDFs)\\n\\nQuestion: Should News & Events be one combined page or two separate sections?\\nResponse: One combined resident-only page: News & Events together\\n\\nQuestion: How sophisticated should the editor be for posting News/updates (keeping it non-technical)?\\nResponse: Rich text: Headings, links, images, and file attachments (still easy)\\n\\nQuestion: For Legal Docs, who should be able to access them?\\nResponse: Public: Anyone can view/download legal documents\\n\\nQuestion: For the Schools page, how detailed should it be?\\nResponse: Simple list of schools with names and links\\n\\nQuestion: How should the Contact Us page work?\\nResponse: Simple form to one recipient inbox\\n\\nQuestion: Should residents get email notifications for new News posts or upcoming Events?\\nResponse: No notifications; residents will check the site\\n\\nQuestion: Do you want a simple site-wide search so residents can quickly find documents and posts?\\nResponse: No, keep it minimal without search\\n\\n---END USER CLARIFICATION HISTORY---\\n\\n---BEGIN DEP---\\nUser Persona\\n- Primary: HOA board member/volunteer with little to no technical background. Goal: publish and maintain essential HOA information with minimal effort; approve resident accounts; manage dues, meetings, and updates without coding.\\n- Secondary: Current residents who need private, up-to-date info (dues, meetings, news/events).\\n- Tertiary: Prospective residents/public seeking general info and legal documents.\\n\\nApp Summary\\nA simple, easy-to-navigate HOA website with a public Home page and core sections. Resident-only access is enforced for Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Admin-friendly tools (non-technical) for posting updates, uploading documents, and approving accounts. No site-wide search and no email notifications for posts/events.\\n\\nUsers & Access\\n- Public (no sign-in): Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us.\\n- Resident-only (sign-in required): Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events.\\n- Account creation: Residents self-register; an admin manually reviews and approves accounts to verify residency. No auto-approval.\\n- Roles:\\n  - Admin: full control (approve users, manage content, manage dues records, upload files).\\n  - Resident: view resident-only pages, manage own profile, make dues payments, view own payment history.\\n\\nPrimary Pages & Requirements\\n1) Home (Public)\\n- Welcoming page with brief community overview, a few photos, and clear quick links to all major sections (including resident-only sections, which prompt sign-in when clicked).\\n- Prominent Sign In and Register buttons.\\n\\n2) Legal Docs (Public)\\n- Simple list of downloadable documents (e.g., CC&Rs, bylaws, policies). Each item shows title and upload/last-updated date.\\n- Optional lightweight grouping by common types (no search).\\n\\n3) Schools (Public)\\n- Simple list of nearby schools with name and outbound link to each school’s site. No maps or extra details.\\n\\n4) Contact Us (Public)\\n- Simple contact form that delivers messages to a single inbox.\\n- Fields: name, email, message. (Phone optional.)\\n- Basic spam protection (non-intrusive) and a success/thank-you message after submission.\\n\\n5) Dues (Resident-only)\\n- Residents can securely pay dues online and see their payment history (dates, amounts, status, and downloadable/printable receipts if available).\\n- Display current balance/status and last payment at a glance.\\n- Admin view to see resident payment records and export/download basic reports if needed. (No automated email reminders; residents must check the site.)\\n\\n6) Annual Meetings (Resident-only)\\n- Upcoming meeting details: date, time, location/virtual link, and brief description.\\n- Past meetings list with downloadable agendas and minutes (PDFs).\\n\\n7) News & Events (Resident-only, combined)\\n- Single combined feed sorted by date (newest first). Entries can be tagged as News or Event.\\n- Event entries include date/time/location fields.\\n- Post editor is easy and non-technical with rich text (headings, links), images, and file attachments.\\n- No email notifications; residents check the site to stay updated.\\n\\nAdmin & Content Management\\n- Non-technical editing experience: create/edit posts, pages, and document listings with a simple rich-text editor; upload PDFs and images.\\n- User approvals: view pending registrations, approve/deny, and deactivate accounts if needed.\\n- Dues management: view payments and history per resident; ability to note manual/offline payments where applicable.\\n- File management: upload/replace PDFs for Legal Docs and Meeting minutes/agendas.\\n\\nNon-Functional Requirements\\n- Simplicity and clarity: clean layout, straightforward navigation, consistent headers/footers.\\n- Mobile-friendly and responsive design.\\n- Accessibility-conscious (e.g., alt text for images, readable contrast, keyboard-friendly navigation).\\n- Security: resident-only content behind sign-in; strong password rules; standard account recovery via email; protect payment and personal data.\\n- Performance: fast-loading pages and images sized appropriately for web.\\n\\nOut of Scope (for now)\\n- Site-wide search.\\n- Email notifications for new posts/events (none requested).\\n- Complex calendars, maps, or advanced directories.\\n\\nSuccess Criteria\\n- The HOA admin can approve residents, post News/Events, upload Legal Docs and Meeting PDFs, and manage Dues without technical help.\\n- Residents can log in, view resident-only content, pay dues online, and see their payment history.\\n- Public visitors can understand the community, access Legal Docs, find local school links, and co